        <h1>Notes from a week without social media</h1>
        <div class="post-meta">
          April 28, 2026 &middot; 5 min read
          <span class="tag" style="margin-top:0;">reflection</span>
        </div>
        <p>I didn't announce it or make it a thing. I just deleted the apps on a Sunday and decided to see what a week felt like without them.</p>
        <p>The first two days were weird. I kept picking up my phone and having nothing to do with it. I noticed how many times a day I reached for it out of pure habit — not boredom, not curiosity, just reflex.</p>
        <p>By day four something shifted. I started finishing things. Books, tasks, conversations. The low-level background noise I didn't know I had went quiet.</p>
        <p>I went back to social media after the week. But I went back differently — less automatically, more deliberately. That felt like enough of a win.</p>
      </div>
